@startuml "Gestion des échecs de paiement - Diagramme de séquence"

title Traitement des webhooks d'échec de paiement

participant "Stripe API" as Stripe
participant "API Gateway\n(Rate Limiter)" as API
participant "Webhook Handler" as WebhookHandler
participant "Payment Service" as PaymentSvc
participant "Order Service" as OrderSvc
participant "Ticket Service" as TicketSvc
participant "Email Service" as EmailSvc
participant "Queue Service\n(Bull/Redis)" as Queue
participant "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB

== Gestion des échecs de paiement ==
Stripe -> API: POST /api/webhook/stripe
note right: Event: payment_intent.payment_failed
API -> WebhookHandler: processStripeWebhook(event)
WebhookHandler -> PaymentSvc: handlePaymentFailed(payment_intent)

PaymentSvc -> DB: SELECT payment WHERE stripePaymentId=?
DB --> PaymentSvc: payment data

PaymentSvc -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
PaymentSvc -> DB: UPDATE payments SET status='failed', failedAt=NOW()
PaymentSvc -> OrderSvc: markOrderAsFailed(orderId)
OrderSvc -> DB: UPDATE orders SET status='payment_failed'
PaymentSvc -> DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION

PaymentSvc -> Queue: addJob('notify-payment-failure', {orderId})
PaymentSvc -> Queue: addJob('release-reserved-tickets', {orderId})

== Libération des billets réservés ==
Queue -> TicketSvc: releaseReservedTickets(orderId)
TicketSvc -> DB: UPDATE tickets SET status='available' WHERE orderId=? AND status='reserved'

== Notification d'échec ==
Queue -> EmailSvc: sendPaymentFailureNotification(orderId)
EmailSvc -> EmailSvc: Send payment failure email with retry link

@enduml